1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,728
Part five: Medications.

2
00:00:03,928 --> 00:00:09,037
The patient's medication list in ThoroughCare must be identical to PointClickCare.

3
00:00:09,077 --> 00:00:13,345
You add every medication from the patient's pharmacy orders.

4
00:00:15,245 --> 00:00:21,718
Each pharmacy order has two parts: the order, which is the medication's name, and the directions.

5
00:00:22,018 --> 00:00:24,277
The name goes in Medication.

6
00:00:24,577 --> 00:00:28,597
Then you read the directions. Give 2 tablet is the dosage.

7
00:00:28,897 --> 00:00:31,424
Two times a day is the frequency.

8
00:00:31,724 --> 00:00:36,314
By mouth is the route, oral. And for pain is the reason taken.

9
00:00:38,314 --> 00:00:41,502
In the assessment menu, open Medications.

10
00:00:41,752 --> 00:00:50,508
The question asks you to review the patient's prescription medications, dietary or herbal supplements, and over-the-counter medicines.

11
00:00:50,758 --> 00:00:57,140
The options are Select from pre-defined list, which is recommended; Enter as free text;

12
00:00:57,180 --> 00:01:02,773
List reviewed in EHR; Patient does not take any medications; and N/A.

13
00:01:03,026 --> 00:01:05,617
Choose Select from pre-defined list.

14
00:01:06,481 --> 00:01:13,125
A medication table opens, with a New Medication button. You'll add the medications one by one.

15
00:01:13,375 --> 00:01:15,731
You'll find them in PointClickCare.

16
00:01:17,047 --> 00:01:20,640
Switch to PointClickCare, and open the Orders tab.

17
00:01:23,781 --> 00:01:31,172
The Orders tab lists all of the patient's orders: pharmacy, diet, laboratory, diagnostic, and other.

18
00:01:31,422 --> 00:01:35,634
You only need the medications. Those are the pharmacy orders.

19
00:01:37,614 --> 00:01:39,706
Open Display Filters.

20
00:01:39,956 --> 00:01:48,982
Under Order Category, every category is checked: Pharmacy, Diet, Supplement, Laboratory, Diagnostic, Other, and Enteral Feed.

21
00:01:49,247 --> 00:01:52,115
Uncheck all of them, except Pharmacy.

22
00:01:56,779 --> 00:01:58,410
Then click Search.

23
00:02:01,147 --> 00:02:05,743
Now the list shows only pharmacy orders: the patient's medications.

24
00:02:05,993 --> 00:02:10,525
Click the Order column heading to sort the medications alphabetically.

25
00:02:10,914 --> 00:02:15,318
Now you can work down the list, and add the medications one by one.

26
00:02:16,647 --> 00:02:24,699
Start with the first medication: Acetaminophen ER Tablet Extended Release 650 MG.

27
00:02:24,949 --> 00:02:28,884
Copy the whole medication name, exactly as it's written.

28
00:02:29,142 --> 00:02:34,634
Then copy the whole directions: Give 2 tablet by mouth two times a day for Pain.

29
00:02:35,947 --> 00:02:39,391
Back in ThoroughCare, go to the medication table.

30
00:02:42,247 --> 00:02:44,112
Click New Medication.

31
00:02:45,247 --> 00:02:52,219
The Add/Edit Medication window opens, with Medication, Prescribed by, Dosage, Frequency, Route,

32
00:02:52,259 --> 00:02:55,859
Reason Taken, Started, Stopped, and Notes.

33
00:02:57,847 --> 00:03:00,912
First, click Notes, and paste the directions.

34
00:03:01,162 --> 00:03:04,391
That way they stay in front of you while you fill in the rest,

35
00:03:04,431 --> 00:03:07,462
and you don't have to go back to PointClickCare.

36
00:03:08,781 --> 00:03:14,550
Next, click Medication, and open your clipboard history with Windows key + V.

37
00:03:14,814 --> 00:03:19,666
Paste the full medication name, exactly as it is in PointClickCare.

38
00:03:20,981 --> 00:03:24,617
Now fill in the rest, using the directions in Notes.

39
00:03:27,425 --> 00:03:30,489
Give 2 tablet: in Dosage, enter 2.

40
00:03:30,739 --> 00:03:32,921
In Units, choose tablets.

41
00:03:33,274 --> 00:03:36,910
Two times a day: in Frequency, choose Twice a day.

42
00:03:40,281 --> 00:03:43,673
By mouth means oral: in Route, choose Oral.

43
00:03:45,581 --> 00:03:48,662
For Pain: in Reason Taken, type Pain.

44
00:03:48,912 --> 00:03:53,124
Leave Prescribed by, Started, and Stopped blank. Click Save.

45
00:03:55,147 --> 00:04:01,322
The medication is added to the table: 2 tablets, twice a day, oral, active, for pain.

46
00:04:01,581 --> 00:04:06,646
Repeat these steps for each and every medication on the pharmacy order list.

47
00:04:06,896 --> 00:04:13,903
Add all of them, until the medication list in ThoroughCare is complete, and identical to PointClickCare.

48
00:04:14,153 --> 00:04:16,765
That completes the Medications section.

49
00:04:18,214 --> 00:04:19,738
Let's recap.

50
00:04:19,938 --> 00:04:27,627
Choose Select from pre-defined list. In PointClickCare, open Orders, filter for Pharmacy, and sort by Order.

51
00:04:27,827 --> 00:04:32,423
Copy each medication's name and directions, exactly as written.

52
00:04:32,623 --> 00:04:38,200
Click New Medication, paste the directions into Notes, and the name into Medication.

53
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:46,239
Read the dosage, frequency, route, and reason from the directions. Then save, and repeat for every medication.

54
00:04:48,439 --> 00:04:52,689
That's part five. The medication list matches PointClickCare.

55
00:04:52,889 --> 00:05:00,258
In part six, the last part, you record the numbers to track: weight, blood pressure, and hemoglobin A1C.
